WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:07.123
A dbt data test is a query that looks for bad rows.

00:00:07.403 --> 00:00:09.617
If it returns nothing, the test passes.

00:00:09.897 --> 00:00:11.594
If it returns rows, it fails.

00:00:12.544 --> 00:00:18.098
dbt has four built in: unique, not null, accepted values, and relationships.

00:00:18.378 --> 00:00:24.355
Start with the grain: the column that should be unique and never empty, like the month in monthly summary.

00:00:25.305 --> 00:00:28.085
Open the project, and open schema dot yml.

00:00:28.365 --> 00:00:30.412
Tests go right under the column they check.

00:00:31.979 --> 00:00:36.541
Under borough, in trips per month: accepted values, with the boroughs we expect.

00:00:38.612 --> 00:00:43.273
Zone id in top pickup zones is that table's grain: not null and unique.

00:00:44.223 --> 00:00:46.359
The same for month in monthly summary.

00:00:46.639 --> 00:00:47.239
Save.

00:00:49.139 --> 00:00:53.171
And in seeds dot yml, Location ID: not null and unique.

00:00:53.451 --> 00:00:54.051
Save.

00:00:58.556 --> 00:01:00.623
Run them all: Project menu, Test.

00:01:03.474 --> 00:01:06.816
Six pass, one fails: accepted values on borough.

00:01:07.096 --> 00:01:09.899
Got one result, so one borough is not in our list.

00:01:10.849 --> 00:01:11.662
It is N A.

00:01:11.942 --> 00:01:21.756
The zone lookup has a zone two sixty-five, outside of New York City, with the borough N A, and about two hundred fifty trips in 2025 started there.

00:01:22.036 --> 00:01:24.130
The data is right; our list was wrong.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.731
Add N A to the list, and save.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:33.939
To check just this model, open trips per month, and in the Model menu choose Test.

00:01:35.497 --> 00:01:37.726
One test on this model, and it passes.

00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:40.214
One more command: build.

00:01:40.494 --> 00:01:46.940
It seeds, runs and tests, in DAG order, so a failing test stops the models that depend on bad data.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:49.125
Project menu, Build.

00:01:50.194 --> 00:01:52.401
One seed, four models, seven tests.

00:01:52.681 --> 00:01:54.294
Twelve passes, no errors.

00:01:55.244 --> 00:01:58.927
The Git tab: schema dot yml and seeds dot yml changed.

00:02:00.195 --> 00:02:03.455
Stage all, type a message, add data tests, and commit.

00:02:08.152 --> 00:02:09.127
Sync Changes.

00:02:09.407 --> 00:02:11.505
That's the end of dbt basics.

00:02:13.252 --> 00:02:16.198
To recap: tests live in YAML next to the columns.

00:02:16.478 --> 00:02:19.289
A failing test told us something true about the data.

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:22.001
And build runs and tests everything, in order.

00:02:22.281 --> 00:02:23.779
That's dbt basics.

00:02:24.059 --> 00:02:28.308
Next, we ship it: GitHub Actions builds the project on every push.
